 "result_text": "`idna.decode(b'\\x8d\\xd2')` now raises `idna.IDNAError` instead of `UnicodeDecodeError`. I didn't run the repo's test suite, only a quick check of the cases below.\n\nThe changes are in `idna/core.py`:\n- **Top-level ASCII decode:** `decode()` now raises `IDNAError('Invalid ASCII in A-label')` when the bytes aren't ASCII. I made the same change in `encode()`, which had the identical unguarded `s.decode('ascii')`.\n- **A-label ending check:** the ASCII decode in `ulabel()` is wrapped the same way.\n- **Punycode decode:** a malformed Punycode string in `ulabel()` now raises `IDNAError('Invalid A-label')`.\n\nI checked `b'\\x8d\\xd2'`, `b'xn--\\x8d'`, `b'xn--a-\\xff'` and `b'xn--zz'`. Each raised `IDNAError`.\n\nI didn't touch the tests or commit anything.",
